course: dictionary
lesson: 12136
title: Words for trade and value
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A commodity is a thing that people buy and sell, or something very useful and valuable. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits. «Countries trade commodities such as oil, wheat and gold.» The clues are trade, buy and sell, so a commodity is a product that is bought and sold.
explain: The second meaning appears in everyday talk. «Clean water is a precious commodity in a dry desert.» Precious tells you the water is very valuable, so commodity here means something useful that people want. Ask yourself: would people think this is worth a lot? If yes, the meaning fits.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping a simpler word into the sentence. Try «Clean water is a precious product in a dry desert.» It still makes sense, so you have found the right idea. Commodity is the word used for goods that are traded.
fact: A commodity is a product or raw material that is bought and sold.
fact: Examples of commodities include wheat, oil, coffee, gold and copper.
fact: «Commodity prices» means the cost of these goods, which can go up and down.
fact: «A precious commodity» means something very valuable that people want, such as «time is a precious commodity».
fact: «The price of wheat rose, so bread cost more in the shops.» Changes in commodity prices can change what we pay in shops.
exercise: «Countries buy and sell commodities such as oil and wheat.» What is a commodity? | *A product or raw material that is bought and sold | A kind of ship that carries goods | A very small amount of money | A type of school subject
exercise: «Clean water is a precious commodity in a dry desert.» What does precious tell you? | *Very valuable | Very cheap | Very cold | Very dirty
exercise: «The price of wheat rose, so bread cost more in the shops.» Find and copy one word that names a commodity. | rose | cost | shops | *wheat
test: «Oil, copper and coffee are all examples of what?» | *Commodities | Lessons | Shops | Rivers
test: «Patience is a rare commodity.» What does this tell the reader? | Patience is a kind of animal | Patience is a place to visit | *Patience is something valuable that people want | Patience is easy to find in every shop
exam: Which sentence uses commodity to mean something useful and valuable that people want? | *«Her time is a precious commodity, so she spends it wisely.» | «The commodity was a red bus that drove past the school.» | «The commodity sang a song at the party.» | «We ate commodity sandwiches on the beach.»
